# Specialist Module Classification Rules

## Specialist modules activate on strong specialist intent only

A module should activate only when the transcript contains **explicit, unambiguous** specialist signals. Weak or incidental mentions must not trigger a specialist path.

## Retaining

Activate retaining only when the transcript describes **retaining a slope, embankment, or grade change** using structural elements (posts, rails, wall panels).

```
// ❌ BAD classifiers — must NOT trigger retaining
"200x50 timber garden bed border"
"keystone edging"
"timber border"
"garden bed renovation"

// ✅ GOOD classifiers — DO trigger retaining
"retaining wall"
"H4 posts at 1m spacing"
"replace the retaining along the back boundary"
```

**Timber alone must not classify a job as retaining.** Timber is also used for garden bed borders, decking, fencing, and edging. Score timber only when it co-occurs with retaining wall context (posts, height, structural wall, slope).

## General landscaping

Jobs with scope + labour + materials + optional works that do not match a specialist trade must be handled by the **general landscaping path** — not forced into retaining, decking, paving, planting, or fencing.

Examples of general landscaping jobs:
- Garden bed renovation / border installation
- Garden bed edging replacement
- Mixed small works without a single dominant trade

## Decking

Timber alone must not classify a job as decking. Decking requires explicit deck structure intent (deck boards, joists, frame, bearer).
